    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1829">

                <pb facs="1468" n="1352" xml:id="pg1352"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 767.70/126.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Ambassador to the Secretary of
                    State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegrams.—Paraphrases.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-11-17">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 17, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Dean of the Diplomatic Corps has just gone to advise the Minister for Foreign
                    Affairs that, in view of the failure of the Turkish Government to state its
                    opinion on the subject within the time agreed upon, the Diplomatic Corps has
                    decided to land about 2,000 men tomorrow to protect the Embassies and
                    Legations.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rockhill.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
